10. COMMIT FIRST, OBSERVE SECOND

One of the fundamental rules of the system is:

«Commit the rules before observing the result.»

The protocol should prevent the rules from being modified after the final result is known.

Flow:

DEFINE RULES
↓
COMMIT EXPECTATION
↓
EXECUTE PROCESS
↓
COLLECT EVIDENCE
↓
VERIFY
↓
COMMIT RESULT
↓
SETTLE

This turns a philosophical idea into a protocol property.

The expectation must be committed before the final result can be used to reinterpret the conditions.

