11. INDUSTRIAL EVIDENCE

Each industrial event can conceptually be represented as:

PROCESS_ID
MACHINE_ID
EVENT_ID
TIMESTAMP
INPUT_COMMITMENT
OUTPUT_COMMITMENT
PREVIOUS_EVENT_HASH
SENSOR_COMMITMENT
MACHINE_SIGNATURE

Events can form a chain:

Event 001 → Event 002 → Event 003 → Event 004

If an earlier event changes, its hash changes.

That change can break subsequent cryptographic references.

Cryptography can demonstrate integrity of the representation.

But integrity does not automatically mean physical truth.

---

12. PROOF-CARRYING INDUSTRIAL DATA

The architecture proposes that industrial data should not circulate simply as:

DATA

but conceptually as:

DATA + SIGNATURE + TIMESTAMP + PREVIOUS COMMITMENT + PROOF

The objective is for information to carry part of the conditions necessary to verify it.

Not:

«“Trust this record.”»

But:

«“Verify this record.”»

This idea can become a central property of the system.

