26. VERIFICATION POOLS

A Verification Pool functions as coordination infrastructure.

It can:

- receive Jobs;
- distribute work;
- coordinate participants;
- collect results;
- measure contributions;
- detect conflicts;
- build commitments;
- prepare settlement.

The architecture does not require a single pool.

Multiple pools can exist.

---

27. COMPETITION BETWEEN POOLS

Pools can compete through:

- efficiency;
- infrastructure;
- availability;
- costs;
- speed;
- tools;
- security;
- workload coverage;
- industrial integration quality.

Industry can select providers according to public and verifiable rules.

The objective is to avoid making coordination dependent on a single mandatory authority.

Competition does not guarantee honesty.

Therefore the protocol should attempt to make the following verifiable:

rules, results, and accounting.

