28. PROOF-OF-WORK AND PROOF-OF-CONTRIBUTION

Two different concepts appear here.

Proof-of-Work

Demonstrates that specified verifiable work was performed.

Proof-of-Contribution

Measures how much verifiable work a participant contributed during an Epoch.

The conceptual relationship is:

«Proof verifies the work.
Contribution accounting measures participation.
Settlement distributes the reward.»

This prevents the proof mechanism from being confused with the economic distribution mechanism.

---

