33. THREAT MODEL

The protocol must assume adversaries.

Among the risks:

Fake Evidence

Generation of false evidence.

Sensor Manipulation

Manipulation of physical data sources.

Replay Attack

Reuse of old evidence.

Duplicate Claim

Two incompatible claims consume the same evidence.

Timestamp Manipulation

Alteration of temporal references.

Pool Collusion

Malicious coordination among operators.

Sybil Participation

Creation of multiple identities to manipulate incentives.

Data Withholding

Strategic withholding of information.

Industrial Censorship

Preventing certain Jobs from being processed.

Verification Fraud

Submitting incorrect computational results in expectation of reward.

The objective is not to promise zero risk.

It is to transform threats into:

detectable, measurable, and verifiable conditions wherever possible.

