34. PERMISSIONLESS VERIFICATION

The traditional question may be:

«“Who are you?”»

The architecture moves toward:

«“Can you prove your contribution?”»

Not:

«“Who controls the pool?”»

But:

«“Are the rules and accounting public and verifiable?”»

Not:

«“Which institution certifies this?”»

But:

«“What evidence can any participant present under the same rules?”»

Identity may still exist.

But evidence gains greater weight as a foundation of trust.

