Industry cannot publish everything.

A useful system must protect proprietary information.

The architecture favors:

- commitments;
- selective disclosure;
- encrypted evidence;
- access-controlled storage;
- zero-knowledge proofs;
- separation between operational data and public data.

The idea is:

«Proof without unnecessary disclosure.»

The blockchain should not become a permanent public record of industrial secrets.

